WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:05.480
Fourteen years is a long time to wait, but
Pixar and writer/director Brad Bird have finally

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:09.509
brought audiences back to the comic book-inspired
world of The Incredibles.

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:13.570
Like any good sequel, it doesn't tie up all
of its plot threads neatly at the end of its

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:14.570
runtime.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:17.699
There's no telling for sure if or when we'll
get a follow-up, so let's take a look at the

00:00:17.699 --> 00:00:20.859
most pressing unanswered questions in Incredibles
2.

00:00:20.859 --> 00:00:22.949
Where's the Underminer?

00:00:22.949 --> 00:00:27.310
Incredibles 2 picks up exactly where the first
movie left off 14 years prior, with the Parr

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:30.230
family facing off against the Underminer.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:33.440
"Behold, the Underminer!"

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.370
The battle rages underground and spills into
the streets as the heroes manage to just barely

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.620
save City Hall.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:42.250
When the dust settles, however, the villain
has escaped, and the Incredibles' failure

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:44.850
to apprehend him kickstarts the rest of the
plot.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.290
So, where has this nemesis vanished to?

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:50.721
The only reference the movie makes to his
whereabouts comes during the credits, when

00:00:50.721 --> 00:00:55.110
the silhouette of his drill vehicle can be
seen driving off into the proverbial sunset.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:59.300
More pressingly, what is he going to buy with
his newly acquired millions?

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:00.940
What was Evelyn's endgame?

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:05.650
Evelyn Deavor reveals her motivation to Elastigirl
in exactly the kind of supervillain monologue

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:07.880
that the first Incredibles film mocked.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.880
"And When I unleash it- You sly dog!

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.420
You got me monologuing!

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.740
I can't believe it."

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:20.570
She blames superheroes for the death of her
father, who relied on the vigilantes even

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:21.820
after they were outlawed.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:26.360
Manipulating her brother's sense of nostalgia,
she intends to frame supers for a terrible

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:29.330
attack and ensure they remain illegal forever.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:33.650
After hypnotizing an entire luxury yacht full
of heroes and world leaders, Evelyn escapes

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:36.550
by plane while the boat steers itself towards
New Urbem.

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:41.740
While the rest of the assembled supers seize
control of the boat, Elastigirl narrowly thwarts

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:42.740
Evelyn's flight.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:44.700
But if she hadn't, what would the villain
have done?

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:45.700
Go into hiding?

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:46.700
Change her name?

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:47.970
We may never know.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:49.930
What's next for the supers?

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:54.830
Incredibles 2 introduces a large cast of never-before-seen
superheroes brought out of hiding by Winston

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:57.159
Deavor as part of his PR campaign.

00:01:57.159 --> 00:01:59.200
Their scenes rank among the movie's highlights.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.560
The real question is: what will they do next?

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.280
Will Voyd get to spend more time with her
idol, Elastigirl?

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:06.890
Will Krushauer ever truly un-crush anything?

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:10.550
Whatever the future holds for each of them,
their chemistry makes it nice to imagine that

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:13.110
they might form a team and continue working
together.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:17.010
Maybe they'll lay the foundations for some
sort of avenging league of justice.

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:18.700
What will Jack-Jack's power be?

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:23.680
Speaking of intriguing superpower combinations,
it's impossible to discuss Incredibles 2 without

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:28.620
bringing up Jack-Jack, whose array of unpredictable
abilities provides many of the movie's most

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:29.870
memorable scenes.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:33.760
When Bob Parr brings his infant son to Edna
Mode to ask for help, she reminds him that

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:38.329
many supers manifest multiple powers early
in life before growing into their defining

00:02:38.329 --> 00:02:39.329
characteristics.

00:02:39.329 --> 00:02:44.049
Jack-Jack, however, has many more powers than
usual for his age, and shows no sign of settling

00:02:44.049 --> 00:02:45.860
into any one of them by the story's end.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:51.659
He remains blessed with laser vision, flammability,
multiplicity, dimension-hopping, and a rage-triggered

00:02:51.659 --> 00:02:52.659
beast mode.

00:02:52.659 --> 00:02:55.579
The only question is what's next for the combustible
baby?

00:02:55.579 --> 00:02:56.709
"Combustion imminent?

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.980
What does that mean?"

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:01.950
"It means fire, Robert."

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.169
What's Honey like?

00:03:03.169 --> 00:03:07.200
The biggest missed opportunity in Incredibles
2 might be the choice to leave Honey Best,

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.419
better known as the wife of Frozone, off-screen
once again.

00:03:10.419 --> 00:03:15.049
The character became an instant fan favorite
in 2004 without even showing her face as she

00:03:15.049 --> 00:03:18.240
refuses to tell Frozone where she put his
supersuit.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.200
"You tell me where my suit is woman!

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.960
We are talking about the greater good!"

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:22.740
"Greater good?

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:23.900
I am your wife!

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:27.189
I am the greatest good you are ever gonna
get!"

00:03:27.189 --> 00:03:30.909
The sequel spends more time with the personal
life of the Parr family, and their friendship

00:03:30.909 --> 00:03:33.529
with "Uncle Lucius" gets more screen time
as well.

00:03:33.529 --> 00:03:37.949
But Honey is once again relegated to a cameo
in voice only as she shouts from across the

00:03:37.949 --> 00:03:38.949
apartment.

00:03:38.949 --> 00:03:39.700
"Suit up.

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:40.700
It might get weird."

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:41.340
"I'll be there.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:41.840
ASAP."

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:43.940
"Where you going ASAP?

00:03:43.949 --> 00:03:45.650
You better be back ASAP."

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:47.879
How long until the next sequel?

00:03:47.879 --> 00:03:51.790
Incredibles 2 throws its audience right back
into the final scene of a movie from nearly

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:53.379
a decade and a half before.

00:03:53.379 --> 00:03:58.080
The gap is so remarkable that Pixar prepared
a special introduction with the cast and crew

00:03:58.080 --> 00:03:59.569
apologizing for the wait.

00:03:59.569 --> 00:04:03.389
So, with all these lingering questions about
the Incredibles universe still hanging in

00:04:03.389 --> 00:04:07.920
the air, we have to ask just one more: will
a third Incredibles ever materialize, and

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:08.920
when?

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:12.499
Considering how long the second film's fate
remained uncertain, the future of the franchise

00:04:12.499 --> 00:04:14.170
is just as unclear as ever.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:15.170
Thanks for watching!

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:18.109
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:18.109 --> 00:04:20.350
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

